{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/36152-peach-assorted-lunar-fixings-for-2-5","id":36152,"title":"PEACH - assorted Lunar fixings for 2.5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-23T22:34:08-08:00","id":36152,"title":"PEACH - assorted Lunar fixings for 2.5","content":"I've been slowly updating Lunar Charms for playability reasons. Welcoming comments and second looks.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">WOLVERINE GAIT (formerly LIGHT-FOOTED MOUNTAIN GOAT STANCE)</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: -- </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mins</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Dexterity 3, Essence 2; </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Type</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Keywords</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Prerequisite Charms</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Graceful Crane Stance</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This is a permanent upgrade to Graceful Crane Stance. The character ignores environmental penalties to movement and actions.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">CAT-FALLING ATTITUDE</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: -- </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mins</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Dexterity 4, Essence 3; </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Type</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Keywords</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Prerequisite Charms</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Graceful Crane Stance</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This is a permanent upgrade to Graceful Crane Stance. Divide the number of yards the character falls by two to determine appropriate damage from falling. The fall does not inflict lethal damage unless the fall covers a distance of at least 50 yards, and the Lunar always lands on her feet.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">MONKEY-LEAP TECHNIQUE</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: -- </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mins</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Dexterity 4, Essence 3; </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Type</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Keywords</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Prerequisite Charms</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Graceful Crane Stance<br /> This is a permanent upgrade to Graceful Crane Stance. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">When using Graceful Crane Stance, the character may take a single jump each turn reflexively, and she doubles the length of all jumps.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">IMPRESSIONS OF STRENGTH</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 2m </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mins</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Strength 3, Essence 3; </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Type</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Reflexive (Step 1)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Keywords</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Combo-OK, Fury-OK</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Prerequisite Charms</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Any Strength Excellency</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Lunars instinctually understand how to do damage, even in situations where normally it would not be possible. Use of this Charm adds one die of post-soak damage and allows damage dice that show 10 to count as two successes. When activated as a part of Relentless Lunar Fury, the Lunar gains the full benefit of this Charm on every attack but must expend motes to access its expansion Charms as normal.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">UNSTOPPABLE LUNAR WOUND</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: -- (+1m) </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mins</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Strength 4, Essence 4; </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Type</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Keywords</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Prerequisite Charms</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Impressions of Strength</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This is a permanent upgrade to Impressions of Strength. Chosen of Luna are capable of inflicting incredible amounts of damage in an instant. For every mote spent, up to (Essence), the Lunar can add three dice of raw damage and a single die of post-soak damage when using Impressions of Strength.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">BIRTH OF FLIGHT TECHNIQUE</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: -- (+1m) </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mins</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Strength 4, Essence 3; </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Type</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Keywords</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Knockback</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Prerequisite Charms</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Impressions of Strength</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This is a permanent upgrade to Impressions of Strength. Stewards are possessed of boundless strength and capable of repelling any foe. By expending a single mote, the Lunar may add (Strength) yards to the knockback effect of their attack. If their attack does not normally provide a knockback effect this activation costs 2m.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> New Charms:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">NINE LIVES UNDERSTANDING</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 1m </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mins</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Perception 3, Essence 2; </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Type</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Reflexive (Step 2)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Keywords</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Combo-OK</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Prerequisite Charms</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Some Lunars have all the luck. Identical to </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Reflex Sidestep Technique</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">FELINE INSIGHT PRANA</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 6m </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mins</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Perception 4, Essence 3; </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Type</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Simple (Speed 5, DV -2)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Keywords</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Combo-OK</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: One scene</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Prerequisite Charms</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Nine Lives Understanding, Eye of the Cat</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The perceptions of cats aren\u2019t limited by mundane distractions, the borders of what might be deemed reality, or the Wyld. As such, a Chosen who learns to emulate the cat\u2019s observational techniques becomes virtually impossible to fool or deceive. A Lunar utilizing Feline Insight Prana adds (Perception) successes in any opposed Awareness check, even if they would not typically be able to discern the presence of the hidden party or object. These successes do not count towards dice caps. This Charm does not allow the Lunar to see through walls or the like.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">WATER OFF A DUCK\u2019S BACK UNDERSTANDING</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 10m </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mins</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Stamina 4, Essence 4; </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Type</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Reflexive (Step 7)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Keywords</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Combo-OK, Obvious</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Prerequisite Charms</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Frenzied Bear Fortification</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">While the urge to resist physical attacks with physical force is natural and laudable, some Chosen of Luna learn that the blase disregard practiced by ducks is a better approach to dealing with such transgressions. The Lunar lets the attack roll off their hardened body. This Charm perfectly negates all damage done to the Lunar post-soak by a single attack. This Charm suffers from the following Flaw of Invulnerability: the Lunar cannot attack anyone or anything until their DV resets twice, with the following caveats; the Lunar may counter-attack anyone who attacks them directly, their Defend Other ward, or someone or something for whom they have an Intimacy, including as designated by Charms such as True-to-the-Pack Dedication.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">WISDOM IN THE MOMENT APPROACH</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: -- (+1wp) </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mins</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Stamina 5, Essence 5; </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Type</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Keywords</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Prerequisite Charms</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Water Off A Duck\u2019s Back Understanding, Wound-Mastering Body Evolution</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This is a permanent upgrade for Water Off A Duck\u2019s Back Understanding. For a surcharge of 1wp, the Lunar can activate Water Off A Duck\u2019s Back Understanding during Step 10 of resolution.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T04:42:38-08:00","id":36295,"title":"","content":"Wolverine Gait looks fine.<br /> <br /> Cat-Falling Attitude seems like it could be better, in comparison to Perfect Poise Stance. Like it should divide the number of yards fallen by (Essence), or something.<br /> <br /> I want to say Monkey-Leap Technique should have a different name, since it's not quite identical to the Solar's MLT.<br /> <br /> The new Impressions of Strength seems fine.<br /> <br /> A technicality: the Cost of Unstoppable Lunar Wound should be +1m+, as you can spend more than one mote. Also on this Charm: Is it meant to be a replacement of the original Unstoppable Lunar Wound? I thought that Charm was pretty good. That and this would synergize really nicely too.<br /> <br /> I know Birth of Flight is based on the original Lunar edge in Impressions of Strength, bit it seems wimpy to me. I feel like it should automatically cause knockback as well, and perhaps be stackable to a degree.<br /> <br /> Nine Lives Understanding should probably be Merged with Wary Swallow Method, as they do the same thing. Also makes me think Nine Lives Understanding should have an appropriate prereq to put it on the same tier as WSM, though hell if I know which, as no canon Charms seem to fit.<br /> <br /> I feel Feline Insight Prana could stand to be a tiny bit cheaper. Like 5m. Also should probably be clearer how it deals with invalid Awareness rolls. Does it make them valid, so you roll and gain successes? Does it make them valid only enough to apply the bonus successes to, but doesn't otherwise allow the Lunar to roll? Is there a default difficulty to finding a thing or person hidden by means of making it invisible (or otherwise imperceptible), or is it treated as visible (or otherwise perceptible) for the purposes of this Charm, (thus most invisible etc things/people would probably be trivial to find unless actually hidden as well)? Making invalid Awareness valid is always weird.<br /> <br /> Water off a Duck's Back Understanding would probably be fine at Essence 3. It's upgrade looks fine too, though I don't even think it needs Wound-Mastering Body Evolution as a prereq.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T05:58:27-08:00","id":36318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/36152-peach-assorted-lunar-fixings-for-2-5?p=36295#post36295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolverine Gait looks fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's there mostly for the sake of completeness. I don't think many people end up taking the terrain mastery Charms. The original name made my eyes bleed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/36152-peach-assorted-lunar-fixings-for-2-5?p=36295#post36295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cat-Falling Attitude seems like it could be better, in comparison to Perfect Poise Stance. Like it should divide the number of yards fallen by (Essence), or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original incarnation was a pretty meh Charm, but I suppose changing it to divide by (Essence) would make it feel more worthy of 10xp. At least it doesn't cost motes any more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/36152-peach-assorted-lunar-fixings-for-2-5?p=36295#post36295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to say Monkey-Leap Technique should have a different name, since it's not quite identical to the Solar's MLT.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hare Hurdles Moon seemed so trite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/36152-peach-assorted-lunar-fixings-for-2-5?p=36295#post36295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new Impressions of Strength seems fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a brief argument about whether it was too weak since the default Charm effect is also its RLF effect and it seems in-bounds, but with the expansions in place it can get pretty wild. +15 raw damage, +6 post-soak damage, 10s count double, and knockback for 8m? I don't think anyone would turn that down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/36152-peach-assorted-lunar-fixings-for-2-5?p=36295#post36295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A technicality: the Cost of Unstoppable Lunar Wound should be +1m+, as you can spend more than one mote. Also on this Charm: Is it meant to be a replacement of the original Unstoppable Lunar Wound? I thought that Charm was pretty good. That and this would synergize really nicely too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and yes; as I opined above stacking the effects of both could generate results that would probably damage the integrity of the game. The one replaces the original.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/36152-peach-assorted-lunar-fixings-for-2-5?p=36295#post36295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know Birth of Flight is based on the original Lunar edge in Impressions of Strength, bit it seems wimpy to me. I feel like it should automatically cause knockback as well, and perhaps be stackable to a degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>As addressed above, when viewed as part of a package it seems much less wimpy, but perhaps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/36152-peach-assorted-lunar-fixings-for-2-5?p=36295#post36295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nine Lives Understanding should probably be Merged with Wary Swallow Method, as they do the same thing. Also makes me think Nine Lives Understanding should have an appropriate prereq to put it on the same tier as WSM, though hell if I know which, as no canon Charms seem to fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Herp. Yeah, WSM should just be Merged and allow Per-based requirements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/36152-peach-assorted-lunar-fixings-for-2-5?p=36295#post36295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel Feline Insight Prana could stand to be a tiny bit cheaper. Like 5m. Also should probably be clearer how it deals with invalid Awareness rolls. Does it make them valid, so you roll and gain successes? Does it make them valid only enough to apply the bonus successes to, but doesn't otherwise allow the Lunar to roll? Is there a default difficulty to finding a thing or person hidden by means of making it invisible (or otherwise imperceptible), or is it treated as visible (or otherwise perceptible) for the purposes of this Charm, (thus most invisible etc things/people would probably be trivial to find unless actually hidden as well)? Making invalid Awareness valid is always weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>It super is. It's a success adder for an opposed Awareness check. Any opposed check. As a bonus, if the Lunar couldn't normally contest for whatever reason, they get to thanks to the Charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/36152-peach-assorted-lunar-fixings-for-2-5?p=36295#post36295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Water off a Duck's Back Understanding would probably be fine at Essence 3. It's upgrade looks fine too, though I don't even think it needs Wound-Mastering Body Evolution as a prereq.</div> </div> </div> </div>WMBE just seemed like a logical jumping off point for figuring out how to negate damage at Step 10 (and it's in the same progression tree).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T07:53:04-08:00","id":37319,"title":"","content":"Now for something totally different.<br /> <br /> I've been running around my head looking for interesting ways for Lunars to supplement their non-physical excellencies. I've got two.<br /> <br /> The first is a direct expenditure-equals-result equation and as such I'm pretty certain it's balanced. Also there are all kinds of crazy caveats with what constitutes a difficulty and what's not, so, yeah.<br /> <br /> The second is an approximately 11.8% improvement in the probability of success on any one die; in actual rolling practice this can feel like a real boom-or-bust Charm, so I've got it tagged as a permanent upgrade to First Excellency.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">NATURAL (ATTRIBUTE) EXPLOITATION</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 2m+ </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mins</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Attribute 4, Essence 4; </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Type</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Reflexive (Step 1 or Step 2)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Keywords</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Combo-OK</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Prerequisite Charms</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Second (Attribute) Excellency</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sometimes you have to cheat to win and Lunars know this best of all. Instead of adding successes to their roll, a Lunar may instead lower the difficulty of the roll by expending 2m per every one fewer success required. This can drop the difficulty to zero and there is no cap on the number of motes that may be spent in conjunction with this Charm. This includes opposed rolls.</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">IMPROBABLE (ATTRIBUTE) APTITUDE</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: -- </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mins</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Attribute 5, Essence 5; </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Type</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Keywords</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Prerequisite Charms</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: First (Attribute) Excellency</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cheating is an art, a pursuit, something that must be mastered on both sides to be truly effective. This Charm allows the Lunar to count all successes that come up \u20189\u2019 on a die as two successes for the purposes of determining roll results. This does not apply to damage rolls unless the Lunar is also using a Charm that allows such use.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T14:27:18-08:00","id":37507,"title":"","content":"Improbable (Attribute) Aptitude is fine, although the last line is unclear. Do you mean &quot;Lunar is using a Charm that also gives 9s as two successes&quot; or &quot;Lunar is using a Charm that gives 10s as 2 successes, and this Charm will make 9s two successes too&quot;. It's also never stated in the Charm that its rolls including the appriopriate Attributes that are enhanced. Technically, you buy this Charm and it'd affect all rolls no matter the Attribute, which I'm pretty sure isn't the intent. Stating that would also make the damage qualifier unnecessary as damage rolls aren't linked to any Attribute (though leaving the qualifier in for clarity's probably not a bad idea).<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's fairly equivalent to Sidereal's World-Shaping Artistic Vision, though being able to buy it for more than one thing makes it very good. On the other hand, yours is E5 vs WSAV at E3.<br /> <br /> Natural (Attribute) Exploitation has issues, I think, mostly stemming from being able to reduce a difficulty to zero. First, while its conceivable I don't even know if it's possible to have a difficulty 0 roll. (Corebook doesn't even mention it as far as I can find.) Second, technically difficulty 0 means you'd need zero successes to succeed in it, meaning you don't even need to roll at all (or your roll doesn't matter). What this results in is that you essentially also negate all penalties, internal and external, making the reduction from difficulty 1 to 0 far better than any other reduction. I'd either drop the diff 0 thing, or make it cost a Willpower to drop it to zero.<br /> <br /> Second is the &quot;This includes opposed rolls.&quot; I'm not sure what you mean by it. If you mean &quot;you can reduce the difficulty of opposed rolls but not the effective number of successes your opponent rolled&quot; then it's fine. Opposed rolls do have difficulties (as well as penalties) besides the opposed successes, after all. Different difficulties between the two in contest, even, like pickpocketing: the thief's difficulty can rise independent of the one trying to spot them. Now if you mean &quot;reduce the number of successes the opponent rolled as if it were a difficulty,&quot; that's a very bad mechanic as it's effectively an uncapped success adder.<br /> <br /> There aren't that many crazy caveats with what constitutes a difficulty, are there? I always though it was just unclear if an ST should make a roll harder with increased difficulty or external penalties, since they effectively do the same thing.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think a Charm that can so generally reduce difficulty could be problematic. Might be better to have it be a Charm that can generally lower penalties? 1m for internal, 2m for external? Still really good. And probably lower mins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}